    ggml : recreate all meta subgraphs after the arena is reallocated
    
    The arena that holds the per-device subgraphs is reallocated when a graph has
    more nodes or more subgraphs than any before. Only the subgraphs of that
    graph were recreated, and at the size of that graph:
    
    - A later graph with more subgraphs, but no more than max_subgraphs, does not
      reallocate and computes through subgraphs that point into the freed arena.
    - A later graph with more nodes than the graph that reallocated, but no more
      than max_nnodes, does not reallocate and overflows the capacity of its
      subgraph.
    
    Recreate all max_subgraphs subgraphs with max_nnodes capacity, which is what
    the arena is sized for. test-alloc runs both sequences with a Meta backend over
    two CPU devices.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-backend-meta.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-backend-meta.cpp
index 86748b689..65f53d0d7 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-backend-meta.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-backend-meta.cpp
@@ -2282,10 +2282,11 @@ static enum ggml_status ggml_backend_meta_graph_compute(ggml_backend_t backend,
                 /*.no_alloc   =*/ true,
             };
             backend_ctx->ctx.reset(ggml_init(params));
+            // the reset frees all main graphs; later graphs within max_subgraphs and max_nnodes do not reset again
             for (size_t j = 0; j < n_backends; j++) {
                 auto & bcj = backend_ctx->backend_configs[j];
-                for (size_t i = 0; i < n_subgraphs; i++) {
-                    bcj.cgraphs[i].cgraph_main = ggml_new_graph_custom(backend_ctx->ctx.get(), cgraph->n_nodes, /*grads =*/ false);
+                for (size_t i = 0; i < backend_ctx->max_subgraphs; i++) {
+                    bcj.cgraphs[i].cgraph_main = ggml_new_graph_custom(backend_ctx->ctx.get(), backend_ctx->max_nnodes, /*grads =*/ false);
                 }
             }
             backend_ctx->cgraphs_aux.resize(n_backends*n_cgraphs_per_device*backend_ctx->max_subgraphs);
